m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: Serine, without stereochemical selection\nOVERALL STRATEGY: Construct a target-centered network from formaldehyde, HCN, ammonia and explicitly identified auxiliary reagents. Ten distinct reaction sequences combine experimentally supported photochemical precursor supply, direct or bisulfite-protected Strecker chemistry, a lower-confidence formamide branch, and glycine hydroxymethylation. These are ten network pathways, not ten independent reaction families or ten experimentally demonstrated continuous syntheses. Photochemical production of serine aminonitrile is distinguished from its subsequent, environmentally less constrained hydrolysis to free serine. Different pH stages require sequential processing rather than one homogeneous reactor. Neutral-parent formulas represent acid-base families; actual cyanide, sulfite, thiophosphate and ammonium speciation is specified in the conditions. Sulfate, phosphate and elemental sulfur provide provisional, atom-balanced donor-side closures for photoredox modules; their exclusive formation is not established by the supplied studies. These closures must not be used to infer measured donor efficiencies. The network includes experimentally motivated destruction branches and exceeds the requested minimum size to represent intermediates and ten pathways explicitly. Unresolved polymeric precursors are not assigned invented molecular structures. No molecular oxygen or biological catalyst is required, and racemic serine is expected.\n\nMOLECULES (28 nodes):\n  - mol_001: H2O (Water) [starting]\n  - mol_002: CH2O (Formaldehyde) [starting]\n  - mol_003: CHN (HCN; aqueous HCN/cyanide reservoir) [starting]\n  - mol_004: H3N (Ammonia; aqueous ammonia/ammonium reservoir) [starting]\n  - mol_005: C2H3NO (Glycolonitrile) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_006: C2H4O2 (Glycolaldehyde) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_007: C3H6N2O (Serine aminonitrile) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_008: C3H8N2O2 (Serinamide) [intermediate]\n  - mol_009: C3H7NO3 (Serine) [target]\n  - mol_010: H2O3S (Neutral-parent representation of aqueous sulfite/bisulfite) [starting]\n  - mol_011: H2O4S (Neutral-parent representation of aqueous sulfate) [intermediate]\n  - mol_012: H3O3PS (Neutral-parent representation of inorganic thiophosphate) [starting]\n  - mol_013: H3O4P (Orthophosphate, neutral-parent representation) [intermediate]\n  - mol_014: S8 (Elemental sulfur) [intermediate]\n  - mol_015: H2S (Hydrogen sulfide; aqueous sulfide reservoir) [starting]\n  - mol_016: C2H6O5S (Glycolaldehyde bisulfite adduct, neutral-parent representation) [intermediate]\n  - mol_017: C2H7NO4S (Glycolaldehyde ammonia-bisulfite adduct, neutral-parent representation) [intermediate]\n  - mol_018: CH3NO (Formamide) [starting]\n  - mol_019: C4H6N2O2 (N-Formylserine aminonitrile) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_020: C4H7NO4 (N-Formylserine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_021: CH2O2 (Formic acid) [intermediate]\n  - mol_022: C2H4N2 (Glycine aminonitrile) [intermediate]\n  - mol_023: C2H6N2O (Glycinamide) [intermediate]\n  - mol_024: C2H5NO2 (Glycine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_025: C4H4N2O (N-Formyldehydroalanine nitrile) [intermediate]\n  - mol_026: C3H5NO2 (Dehydroalanine) [intermediate]\n  - mol_027: H2 (Hydrogen) [starting]\n  - mol_028: C3H7NO2 (Alanine