sulfide photoreduction supplies glycolaldehyde, which is promptly combined with ammonia and cyanide without a storage stage. Serine formation then requires the explicitly proposed amide-resolved hydrolysis and cooling sequence. The complete staged sequence is not experimentally demonstrated.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_005", "rxn_011", "rxn_012"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_008", "mol_009", "mol_010", "mol_011"]}, {"pathway_id": "P2", "name": "Copper-sulfide carbonyl production with bisulfite storage", "description": "The same photochemical carbonyl source is followed by covalent bisulfite storage and formation of the experimentally supported ammonia-bisulfite adduct before cyanide addition. This is a storage-dependent alternative to P1, not an independent carbon-skeleton mechanism. Compatibility of residual copper/sulfur species with the storage sequence remains to be tested.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008", "rxn_011", "rxn_012"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_008", "mol_009", "mol_013", "mol_014", "mol_010", "mol_011"]}, {"pathway_id": "P3", "name": "Sulfite-ferrocyanide carbonyl production followed by immediate Strecker conversion", "description": "Glycolonitrile enters sulfite-ferrocyanide photoreduction. Glycolaldehyde is captured in a separately adjusted ammoniacal Strecker stage rather than relying on in situ photochemical aminonitrile formation. Photon dose, carbonyl survival, mixing dilution and subsequent hydrolysis control the achievable flux.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_003", "rxn_005", "rxn_011", "rxn_012"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_008", "mol_009", "mol_010", "mol_011"]}, {"pathway_id": "P4", "name": "Sulfite-ferrocyanide carbonyl production with bisulfite storage", "description": "Photogenerated glycolaldehyde is trapped before concentration or delayed use. Sulfite/bisulfite has distinct roles as upstream reductant and downstream reversible carbonyl-trapping reagent; suffi